[[Gubernatorial elections]] are scheduled to be held in the [[United States]] on November 3, 2026. This election will take place in 36 states and three territories. The previous gubernatorial elections for this group of states took place in [[2022 United States gubernatorial elections|2022]], except in [[New Hampshire]] and [[Vermont]], where governors serve two-year terms and elected their governors in [[2024 United States gubernatorial elections|2024]]. 

Fifteen of the thirty-six states and two of the three United States territories with elections in this cycle have officially [[Term limits in the United States|term-limited]] incumbents.

== Partisan composition ==
{{unsourced section|date=October 2026}}
Going into the election, there are 26 [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] governors and 24 [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] governors in the United States. This class of governors is made up of 18 Republicans and 18 Democrats. Republicans are defending two governorships in states that [[Kamala Harris]] won in 2024 (New Hampshire and Vermont). Democrats are defending five governorships in states that [[Donald Trump]] won in 2024 (Arizona, Kansas, Michigan, Pennsylvania, and Wisconsin).

== Retirements ==
There are 22 incumbent governors (11 Democrats, 10 Republican, and one Independent) retiring, of which 17 incumbent governors (eight Democrats and nine Republicans) are term-limited. The remaining five incumbent governors (three Democrats, one Republican, and one Independent) have announced they are not seeking reelection.

===Democratic===
#[[California]]: [[Gavin Newsom]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Colorado]]: [[Jared Polis]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Washington, D.C.|District of Columbia]]: [[Muriel Bowser]] is retiring.<ref name="Bowserretirement"/>
#[[Guam]]: [[Lou Leon Guerrero]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Kansas]]: [[Laura Kelly]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Maine]]: [[Janet Mills]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Michigan]]: [[Gretchen Whitmer]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Minnesota]]: [[Tim Walz]] is retiring.<ref name="Walz26"/>
#[[New Mexico]]: [[Michelle Lujan Grisham]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[United States Virgin Islands]]: [[Albert Bryan Jr.]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Wisconsin]]: [[Tony Evers]] is retiring.<ref name="Evers"/>

===Republican===
#[[Alabama]]: [[Kay Ivey]] is term-limited after 2 full terms.
#[[Alaska]]: [[Mike Dunleavy (politician)|Mike Dunleavy]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Florida]]: [[Ron DeSantis]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Georgia (U.S. state)|Georgia]]: [[Brian Kemp]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Iowa]]: [[Kim Reynolds]] is retiring.<ref name="Reynolds">{{cite news |last1=Howell |first1=Michael |title=Kim Reynolds announces she won't seek reelection in 2026 |url=https://cbs2iowa.com/news/local/kim-reynolds-announces-she-wont-seek-reelection-in-2026 |access-date=April 11, 2025 |work=[[CBS 2 Iowa]] |date=April 11, 2025}}</ref>
#[[Ohio]]: [[Mike DeWine]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
#[[Oklahoma]]: [[Kevin Stitt]] is term-limited after 2 terms.
