U.S. Senator [[Marsha Blackburn]],<ref name="BlackburnTN">{{cite news |last1=Taylor |first1=Sarah Grace |title=Marsha Blackburn announces run for Governor of Tennessee |url=https://nashvillebanner.com/2025/08/06/marsha-blackburn-tennessee-governor-campaign-launch/ |access-date=August 6, 2025 |work=Nashville Banner |date=August 6, 2025}}</ref> state representative [[Monty Fritts]],<ref name="FrittsTN">{{cite news |last1=Grace Taylor |first1=Sarah |title=State Rep. Monty Fritts announces 2026 governor run |url=https://nashvillebanner.com/2025/09/08/ascend-amphitheater-opry-entertainment-group/ |access-date=September 8, 2025 |work=Nashville Banner |date=September 8, 2025}}</ref> and U.S. Representative for [[Tennessee's 6th congressional district]] [[John Rose (Tennessee politician)|John Rose]]<ref name="Rose">{{Cite web |title=Rose tells friends, supporters he's on go for 2026 governor's race |url=https://pro.stateaffairs.com/tn/elections/rose-tennessee-governor |access-date=January 27, 2025 |website=State Affairs |language=en}}</ref> ran for the Republican nomination. Blackburn won the nomination with 43.4% of the vote on August 6.

For the Democrats, [[Memphis City Council|Memphis city councilor]] Jerri Green<ref name="GreenTN">{{Cite web |last=Finton |first=Lucas |date=July 14, 2025 |title=Memphis City Councilwoman Jerri Green officially throws hat into Tennessee governor's race |url=https://www.commercialappeal.com/story/news/local/2025/07/14/memphis-city-councilwoman-jerri-tennessee-governor/85191204007/ |access-date=July 17, 2025 |website=[[The Commercial Appeal]] |language=en-US}}</ref> defeated leader of New Chicago Community Development Corporation and 2022 candidate for governor [[Carnita Atwater]], nominee for the 109th district in the [[Illinois House of Representatives]] in [[2010 Illinois House of Representatives election|2010]] Tim Cyr, and guitarist Adam Kurtz for the nomination.<ref name="Contested">{{cite web |last1=Cornell |first1=Josh |date=September 16, 2025 |title=The Civic Scoop: Cornell on the ongoing Tennessee governor's race |url=https://highlandecho.com/the-civic-scoop-cornell-on-the-ongoing-tennessee-governors-race/ |access-date=September 16, 2025 |website=[[The Highland Echo]] |quote=There are also four democrats running for this position: Jerri Green, Carnita Atwater, Adam Kurtz, and Tim Cyr...}}</ref> 

Former [[Lipscomb University]] professor Lauren Pinkston is running as an independent.<ref name="Pinkston">{{Cite web |last=Rayner |first=Ruby |date=November 21, 2025 |title=Lauren Pinkston, an independent running for Tennessee governor, wants to give people a third option |url=https://www.timesfreepress.com/news/2025/nov/21/former-lipscomb-university-professor-launches-bid/ |access-date=November 24, 2025 |website=[[Chattanooga Times Free Press]] |language=en-US}}</ref>
