{{Main|2026 United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election}}

Governor [[Albert Bryan (politician)|Albert Bryan]] was re-elected in [[2022 United States Virgin Islands gubernatorial election|2022]] with 56.1% of the vote. He will be term limited in 2026 and cannot seek re-election for a third consecutive term.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-02-20 |title=In Washington, USVI Gov. Bryan Pushes Administration for Tariff Relief and Reflects on Two Terms of Service |url=https://usvinews.tv/news/in-washington-usvi-gov-bryan-pushes-administration-for-tariff-relief-and-reflects-on-two-terms-of-service/ |access-date=2026-03-28 |website=[[WCVI-TV]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

Current [[Delegate (United States Congress)|delegate]] to the [[United States House of Representatives]] [[Stacey Plaskett]] defeated [[Lieutenant Governor of the United States Virgin Islands|Lieutenant Governor]] [[Tregenza Roach]] and former [[Legislature of the Virgin Islands|senator]] [[Donna Frett-Gregory]] in the primary.<ref name=Frett-GregoryVI>{{cite web |last1=Eader |first1=Tom |title=Ex-Sen. Donna Frett-Gregory picks up papers to enter governor's race as 2026 field continues to grow |url=https://newsfeed.wtjx.org/podcast/wtjx-newsfeed/2026-04-17/ex-sen-donna-frett-gregory-picks-up-papers-to-enter-governors-race-as-2026-field-continues-to-grow |publisher=[[WTJX-TV]] |access-date=April 27, 2026 |date=April 17, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Burgher |first1=Vernice |title=Plaskett-Porter launches bid for Government House in historic Frederiksted |url=https://www.virginislandsdailynews.com/news/plaskett-potter-launches-bid-for-government-house-in-historic-frederiksted/article_a9a5bd28-f738-4285-974f-422255ffc466.html |access-date=April 20, 2026 |publisher=[[Virgin Islands Daily News]] |date=April 19, 2026 |language=en}}</ref><ref name=RoachVI>{{cite web |last1=Eader |first1=Tom |title=Lt. Gov. Roach picks up gubernatorial papers as new candidates enter Senate and congressional races |url=https://newsfeed.wtjx.org/2026-04-16/lt-gov-roach-picks-up-gubernatorial-papers-as-new-candidates-enter-senate-and-congressional-races |publisher=[[WTJX-TV]] |access-date=April 27, 2026 |date=April 16, 2026}}</ref>

Plaskett will face Former [[Saint Croix]] police chief and senator Oakland Benta, former Democratic senator [[Adlah Donastorg Jr.]], former public works commissioner Gustav James, and hedge fund executive [[Warren Mosler]], who are running as independents in the general election.<ref name=BentaVI>{{cite web |last1=Eader |first1=Tom |title=Ex-Sen. Oakland Benta picks up gubernatorial papers; Raymond Williams barred from seeking reelection |url=https://newsfeed.wtjx.org/podcast/wtjx-newsfeed/2026-04-21/ex-sen-oakland-benta-picks-up-gubernatorial-papers-raymond-williams-barred-from-seeking-reelection |publisher=[[WTJX-TV]] |access-date=April 28, 2026 |date=April 21, 2026}}</ref><ref name=IndependentsVI>{{cite web |last1=Eader |first1=Tom |title=Independents show interest in gubernatorial race as more aspirants pick up elected office petitions |url=https://newsfeed.wtjx.org/podcast/wtjx-newsfeed/2026-04-16/independents-show-interest-in-gubernatorial-race-as-more-aspirants-pick-up-elected-office-petitions |publisher=[[WTJX-TV]] |access-date=April 28, 2026 |date=April 16, 2026}}</ref><ref name=FrettJohnHopeVI>{{cite web |last1=Eader |first1=Tom |title=Ex-Sen. Stephen Frett, Jed JohnHope pick up gubernatorial petitions; McClafferty eyes Congress seat |url=https://newsfeed.wtjx.org/podcast/wtjx-newsfeed/2026-04-25/ex-sen-stephen-frett-jed-johnhope-pick-up-gubernatorial-petitions-mcclafferty-eyes-congress-seat |publisher=[[WTJX-TV]] |access-date=April 28, 2026 |date=April 25, 2026}}</ref><ref name=Mosler>{{cite web|url= https://viconsortium.com/vi-politics/virgin-islands-warren-mosler-announces-bid-for-governor--promises--20-000-to--25-000-payments-to-registered-voters|title= Warren Mosler Announces Bid For Governor, Promises $20,000 to $25,000 Payments to Registered Voters|date=February 4, 2026|access-date=February 5, 2026|work=The Virgin Islands Consortium|author=Ernice Gilbert}}</ref>
